    'The field is the force per unit charge on a small positive test charge. A field of zero at a point does not mean zero potential: between two equal like charges the field is zero at the midpoint but the potential is not. The field points away from positive charge and towards negative charge, and falls with the square of the distance. For the potential at the same point use the Electric Potential Calculator. This is an idealised textbook model; it is not a field simulation of real electrodes, and no breakdown or corona limit is checked.',
